---
import Layout from "../layouts/layout.astro";
---

<Layout
    title="About | Gabby"
    description="About Gabriele Naseviciute, a senior graphic designer and creative technologist."
>
    <section class="page-intro">
        <p class="eyebrow">About</p>

        <h1>Designer first. Technologist second. AI nerd underneath.</h1>

        <p>
            I'm Gabby, a senior graphic designer with more than 11 years of
            experience across visual communication, digital design and web.
        </p>

        <p>
            Alongside the design work, I write code. Python, AI and software,
            mostly aimed at practical systems that take on the jobs nobody
            likes.
        </p>
    </section>

    <div class="about-sections">
        <section class="about-section">
            <h2>What I do</h2>
            <div class="about-section-body">
                <h3>Design</h3>
                <p>
                    I take complicated, wordy things like brand guidelines and policy
                    documents and make them clear, engaging and a pleasure to read. After 11
                    years across platforms, my edge is the unglamorous bit: before any draft
                    goes to a client, I check the spacing. Guides, grids, headers, footers,
                    tracking, everywhere, every time. My favourite briefs are the ones that
                    look dry on the surface.
                </p>

                <h3>Technology</h3>
                <p>
                    My first line of code was a tweak to a WordPress footer, because the
                    spacing bothered me. It took a lot of Googling, and by the end I
                    thought: this isn't that hard. Now I'm building a locally hosted AI agent
                    that drafts site-specific planning documents in a company's tone, using
                    a library of past precedents. Being a designer helps: I know what the
                    person on the other side of the screen needs, and I care how the finished
                    thing looks.
                </p>
                <p>
                    I think design should stay with designers and AI should take the jobs
                    nobody likes doing. For designers, it's one of the most useful tools in
                    years.
                </p>

            </div>
        </section>

         <section class="about-section">
            <h2>Skills and tools</h2>
            <div class="about-section-body">
                <p>I know most of the shortcuts, and I'm working on the rest.</p>

                <h3>Design</h3>
                <ul class="about-list">
                    <li>Adobe Suite: Photoshop, Illustrator, InDesign</li>
                    <li>Figma</li>
                    <li>Branding, logos and brand guidelines</li>
                    <li>Print-ready artwork, from flyers to billboards</li>
                    <li>Infographics and planning graphics</li>
                    <li>Product photography and retouching</li>
                </ul>

                <h3>Code and AI</h3>
                <ul class="about-list">
                    <li>HTML, CSS and JavaScript</li>
                    <li>Astro</li>
                    <li>Git and GitHub</li>
                    <li>Python</li>
                    <li>Local LLMs and RAG</li>
                    <li>Streamlit</li>
                    <li>Docker</li>
                    <li>Markdown</li>
                    <li>Wordpress and SEO</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="about-section">
            <h2>Experience</h2>
            <div class="about-section-body">
                <p>
                    Print is where I started and what I've done the most of:
                    brochures, flyers, vehicle graphics. It has since widened
                    to branding, social, TV and web graphics, public
                    consultation material and planning documents.
                </p>

                <ol class="timeline" role="list">
                    <li class="timeline-item">
                        <p class="timeline-years">2025–now</p>
                        <div>
                            <h3 class="timeline-role">Senior Graphic Designer</h3>
                            <p class="timeline-org">Pegasus Group, Urban Design team</p>
                            <p>
                                Design and Access Statements, promotional
                                material and planning graphics that make
                                complex proposals easy to follow.
                            </p>
                        </div>
                    </li>

                    <li class="timeline-item">
                        <p class="timeline-years">2022–2025</p>
                        <div>
                            <h3 class="timeline-role">Design and Digital Lead</h3>
                            <p class="timeline-org">THIRTY 4/7 Communications, joined as Graphic Designer</p>
                            <p>
                                Public consultation design from start to
                                finish, from roller banners and forms to
                                WordPress and SEO. Later led the design
                                process, suppliers and website performance.
                            </p>
                        </div>
                    </li>

                    <li class="timeline-item">
                        <p class="timeline-years">2021–2022</p>
                        <div>
                            <h3 class="timeline-role">Graphic Designer</h3>
                            <p class="timeline-org">Urban Inprint</p>
                            <p>
                                Brochures, presentations and infographics,
                                colourised architectural drawings, WordPress
                                and social media for two brands.
                            </p>
                        </div>
                    </li>

                    <li class="timeline-item">
                        <p class="timeline-years">2019–2021</p>
                        <div>
                            <h3 class="timeline-role">Lead Graphic Designer and Photographer</h3>
                            <p class="timeline-org">Deramores, one of the UK's largest yarn retailers</p>
                            <p>
                                Web and print, advertising, branding,
                                packaging and product photography, often
                                several projects at once.
                            </p>
                        </div>
                    </li>

                    <li class="timeline-item">
                        <p class="timeline-years">2017–2019</p>
                        <div>
                            <h3 class="timeline-role">Graphic Designer</h3>
                            <p class="timeline-org">Flexi Print Shop</p>
                            <p>
                                Logos, flyers and billboards, plus setting up
                                the large-format printer and training junior
                                staff.
                            </p>
                        </div>
                    </li>

                    <li class="timeline-item">
                        <p class="timeline-years">2015–2017</p>
                        <div>
                            <h3 class="timeline-role">Graphic Designer</h3>
                            <p class="timeline-org">Mimeo UK</p>
                            <p>
                                Print-ready artwork to strict brand guidelines
                                on three-hour turnarounds.
                            </p>
                        </div>
                    </li>
                </ol>

                <!-- CV download link goes here once the PDF is ready -->
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="about-section">
            <h2>Contact</h2>
            <div class="about-section-body">
                <p>
                    Say hello on LinkedIn, or have a look at how this site is
                    built on GitHub.
                </p>

                <ul class="about-list">
                    <li>
                        <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/gnaseviciute/">LinkedIn</a>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <a href="https://github.com/just-gabby">GitHub</a>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </section>
    </div>
</Layout>